From 14fe6005060354374d3e2ce42f8952772b514001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:35:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Walk up the tree to find an inherited interrupt parent

Without an `interrupt-parent` property, the devicetree parent was returned
as interrupt parent even when it is a plain bus node without
`#interrupt-cells`. Follow `interrupt-parent` links and devicetree parents
until an interrupt controller is found, like Linux's `of_irq_find_parent`.

This broke parsing `interrupts` of the GPIO controller on the Raspberry Pi 3
and Zero 2 W, whose `/soc` node inherits `interrupt-parent` from the root.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
